+    // ------------------------------------------------------------------
+    // SPARK simulator patch: synchronous GC via a manual Asyncify unwind/rewind.
+    //
+    // gc_collect() (main.c) calls mp_js_gc_spill_and_scan().  That starts an
+    // Asyncify unwind, which spills the locals of every active wasm frame into
+    // the buffer at $MPGC.data and returns all the way to the JS->C entry point.
+    // The entry point is wrapped by $MPGC.wrap (installed by api.js); the wrapper
+    // stops the unwind, lets C scan the spilled locals (mp_js_gc_scan_region)
+    // and rewinds the stack by calling the entry point again.  The rewind ends
+    // in mp_js_gc_spill_and_scan(), which stops it, and gc_collect() continues.
+    // Everything happens synchronously inside the original call, so long-running
+    // code (a robot program in a `while True:` loop) gets real collections and a
+    // hard heap limit.
+    //
+    // Unwinding through a JS frame is only safe for stateless trampolines
+    // (emscripten's invoke_* functions for setjmp/longjmp).  If Python is entered
+    // again from JS that was called from Python (depth > 1), the outer frames
+    // cannot be spilled and gc_collect() skips the collection.
